Rings
=====

Many rings are suitable for special situations - for a complete list of
rings and the intrinsics granted, see
  http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/ring-343.txt
  http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/rint-343.txt
and
  http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/drgn-343.txt

A few of the rings are very helpful. These include:
 o ring of conflict to cause monsters to attack each other (and
peaceful monsters may attack you!). There are some special cases, but
generally do not use if you have strong pets or until you can handle
the adverse effects. Some have said that a ring of conflict is worth
several levels of AC since many monsters will attack other monsters
instead of you. There are also situations (e.g., the Big Room, Castle,
Ludios, the Planes) where a ring of conflict can thin out the enemies
so you have less hostile monsters to kill. Note that this ring
increases your hunger by 50%, so have plenty of food when you use it.
 o ring of free action to prevent or reduce paralysis and stunning
attacks to a single turn. This is especially helpful in the middle to
late game because many spell using monsters can cast those spells. This
ring is worn in many nethack ascensions.
 o if you find one, a ring of poison resistance is particularly helpful
in the early game to prevent an untimely death (a variety of poison
causes). If you wear one of these while eating a monster granting
poison resistance, you won't die (unless extremely weak or satiated),
giving you several opportunities to get poison resistance without
having to use a ring slot.
 o ring of teleport control to control where you teleport. Particularly
helpful in level teleports to rapidly move across levels. Also helpful
for teleports within the level in most cases - an exception is if you
are looking for a vault, remove it before triggering a vault teleport
trap (so you go directly to the vault).

Other rings provide benefits in certain situations. Most of these
provide intrinsics that can be granted in other ways (see the spoilers
referenced above) and will not be helpful in the late game. I do not
recommend using these if you need to use the ones listed above.
 o ring of levitation to float over traps, water, lava, and holes
(except in Sokoban). Note that levitation prevents several common
activities and does not prevent water monsters from drowning you.
 o ring of stealth to prevent sleeping monsters from waking (except for
a few exceptions).
 o ring of (cold, fire, or shock) resistance can be used until you get
the resistance by eating the right kind of monster.
 o ring of warning to help locate non-trivial monsters near you.
 o ring of slow digestion is helpful in the early game (before you have
LOTS of food) but less helpful later.
 o ring of see invisible if you don't have the intrinsic any other way.
 o ring of protection from shape changers is helpful against the shape
changing monsters and prevents lycanthropy or summoning by
were-animals, may help in the early game or in the Rogue quest.
 o ring of searching to help find traps, secret doors, and "hidden"
monsters.

Some rings that could be considered "traps" include:
 o ring of aggravate monster is often cursed and tends to wake up
sleeping monsters (unless stealthy).
 o ring of hunger is often cursed and increases hunger by 50%. However,
note that hunger can be helpful if you are Satiated and want to remove
that sooner.
 o ring of invisibility provides temporary invisibility. The hard
monsters can all "see invisible" so it doesn't help for the mid to end
game.
 o ring of polymorph has a 1% chance each turn to change your form and
is often cursed. With poly control, it can be used effectively, but is
generally helpful in limited cases (e.g., poly to a Xorn to help
complete the Rogue quest).
 o ring of regeneration provides an HP boost each turn. Yes the HP
increase is nice, but the hunger effects can kill you if you lack food
and the HP boost is helpful only in the early game (before you have
LOTS of food).

